prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-array.prototype.sort spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1 ref:ucaimplicit@1
script: (function(c,w){w.sort(c.compare);var s=w[0];for(var i=1;i<w.length;i++)s+=" "+["<","=",">"][Math.sign(c.compare(w[i-1],w[i]))+1]+" "+w[i];return s})(new Intl.Collator("en"),["a","z","\u00DF","ss","\u00E6","ae","\u00F8","\u0153","\u00FE","\u00F0","\u0131","\u03B1","\u03C9","\u0430","\u044F","\u10D0","\u0561","\u05D0","\u05EA","\u0627","\u064A","\u0905","\u0939","\u0E01","\u0E2E","\uAC00","\uD7A3","\u3042","\u30A2","\u3093","\u4E00","\u4E01","\u4E2D","\uD840\uDC00","\uD83D\uDE00","1","\u0661","\u0967","\u00BD","\u2460","\u13A0","\u1200","\u0F40","\u1820","\uA000"])
note: 45 strings sorted under en, each neighbour's relation written between them: rows O1 and O3 (O1 data policy, C5; O3 data policy, C5): CLDR 48.2.0's root over Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, Georgian, Armenian, Hebrew, Arabic, Devanagari, Thai, Hangul, kana, Cherokee, Ethiopic, Tibetan, Mongolian, Yi, Han across two blocks, an emoji, digits of three scripts and two compatibility digits; the answer moves with the order of Han characters, which UTS #35 Part 5 (CLDR 48) leaves to the implementation ("an implementation may choose either to implement the order defined in the UCA and the [Unified_Ideograph] data, or to implement the order defined by the [radical ...] lines"), and which ECMA-402 does not fix: out is the reference's, by radical and stroke; each engine's expectation is its own collation data's answer (the owner's decision of 2026-11-02, JSD-0084): Broiler.VM's, its tables' UCA 17 implicit weights over allkeys_CLDR.txt (ref:ucaimplicit@1), and Broiler.JS's, its host's ICU by radical and stroke, which is out; neither is a correction, and finding F1 stays open for SJL-17.3 (row O3, data policy, C5)
since: 33

