prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1 ref:ucaimplicit@1
script: ["<","=",">"][Math.sign(new Intl.Collator("en").compare("\uD840\uDC00","\u4E2D"))+1]
note: U+D840U+DC00 against U+4E2D under en: rows O1 and O3 (O1 data policy, C5; O3 data policy, C5): neighbours in the reference's order of the scripts' sort, CLDR 48.2.0's root; the answer moves with the order of Han characters, which UTS #35 Part 5 (CLDR 48) leaves to the implementation ("an implementation may choose either to implement the order defined in the UCA and the [Unified_Ideograph] data, or to implement the order defined by the [radical ...] lines"), and which ECMA-402 does not fix: out is the reference's, by radical and stroke; each engine's expectation is its own collation data's answer (the owner's decision of 2026-11-02, JSD-0084): Broiler.VM's, its tables' UCA 17 implicit weights over allkeys_CLDR.txt (ref:ucaimplicit@1), and Broiler.JS's, its host's ICU by radical and stroke, which is out; neither is a correction, and finding F1 stays open for SJL-17.3 (row O3, data policy, C5)
since: 33

id: intl/collation/root/punctuation/0001
area: intl
op: Array.prototype.sort with Intl.Collator.prototype.compare
in: str:"en" str:" " str:"_" str:"-" str:"," str:";" str:":" str:"!" str:"?" str:"." str:"'" str:"\"" str:"(" str:")" str:"[" str:"@" str:"*" str:"/" str:"\\" str:"&" str:"#" str:"%" str:"`" str:"^" str:"+" str:"<" str:"=" str:"|" str:"~" str:"$" str:"\u20AC" str:"0" str:"a"
out: value: str:"  < _ < - < , < ; < : < ! < ? < . < ' < \" < ( < ) < [ < @ < * < / < \\ < & < # < % < ` < ^ < + < < < = < | < ~ < $ < \u20AC < 0 < a"
class: normative
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-array.prototype.sort spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1
script: (function(c,w){w.sort(c.compare);var s=w[0];for(var i=1;i<w.length;i++)s+=" "+["<","=",">"][Math.sign(c.compare(w[i-1],w[i]))+1]+" "+w[i];return s})(new Intl.Collator("en"),[" ","_","-",",",";",":","!","?",".","'","\"","(",")","[","@","*","/","\\","&","#","%","`","^","+","<","=","|","~","$","\u20AC","0","a"])
note: 32 strings sorted under en, each neighbour's relation written between them: row O1 (data policy, C5): the root's order of spaces, punctuation, symbols, a digit and a letter, non-ignorable
since: 33

