out: value: str:"\u4E00 < \u4E01 < \u4E02 < \uD840\uDC00 < \uD840\uDC01 < \uD873\uDEB0 < \uD880\uDC00 < \uD869\uDF00 < \uD86D\uDF40 < \uD888\uDFB0 < \uD87A\uDFF0 < \u3400 < \uD884\uDF50 < \u3401 < \uD87E\uDC00 < \u4E2D < \u4EBA < \uFA0E < \uFA0F < \u5B50 < \uFA11 < \uD86E\uDC20 < \u6C34 < \u9FCC < \u9FFF < \u9FA6 < \u9FEA < \uD869\uDEDF < \uFA1F < \uF900 < \uFA29 < \u4DBF < \u9F9C < \u9FA5 < \u4DB5"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"\u4E00 < \u4E01 < \u4E02 < \uD840\uDC00 < \uD840\uDC01 < \uD873\uDEB0 < \uD880\uDC00 < \uD869\uDF00 < \uD86D\uDF40 < \uD888\uDFB0 < \uD87A\uDFF0 < \u3400 < \uD884\uDF50 < \u3401 < \uD87E\uDC00 < \u4E2D < \u4EBA < \uFA0E < \uFA0F < \u5B50 < \uFA11 < \uD86E\uDC20 < \u6C34 < \u9FCC < \u9FFF < \u9FA6 < \u9FEA < \uD869\uDEDF < \uFA1F < \uF900 < \uFA29 < \u4DBF < \u9F9C < \u9FA5 < \u4DB5"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"\u4E00 < \u4E01 < \u4E02 < \u4E2D < \uD87E\uDC00 < \u4EBA < \u5B50 < \u6C34 < \uF900 < \u9F9C < \u9FA5 < \u9FA6 < \u9FCC < \u9FEA < \u9FFF < \uFA0E < \uFA0F < \uFA11 < \uFA1F < \uFA29 < \u3400 < \u3401 < \u4DB5 < \u4DBF < \uD840\uDC00 < \uD840\uDC01 < \uD869\uDEDF < \uD869\uDF00 < \uD86D\uDF40 < \uD86E\uDC20 < \uD873\uDEB0 < \uD87A\uDFF0 < \uD880\uDC00 < \uD884\uDF50 < \uD888\uDFB0"
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-array.prototype.sort spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1 ref:ucaimplicit@1
script: (function(c,w){w.sort(c.compare);var s=w[0];for(var i=1;i<w.length;i++)s+=" "+["<","=",">"][Math.sign(c.compare(w[i-1],w[i]))+1]+" "+w[i];return s})(new Intl.Collator("en"),["\u4E00","\u4E01","\u4E02","\u4E2D","\u4EBA","\u5B50","\u6C34","\u9F9C","\u9FA5","\u9FA6","\u9FCC","\u9FEA","\u9FFF","\uFA0E","\uFA0F","\uFA11","\uFA1F","\uFA29","\u3400","\u3401","\u4DB5","\u4DBF","\uD840\uDC00","\uD840\uDC01","\uD869\uDEDF","\uD869\uDF00","\uD86D\uDF40","\uD86E\uDC20","\uD873\uDEB0","\uD880\uDC00","\uD884\uDF50","\uD87A\uDFF0","\uD888\uDFB0","\uF900","\uD87E\uDC00"])
note: 35 strings sorted under en, each neighbour's relation written between them: row O3 (data policy, C5): Han across blocks (finding F1): the reference orders them by radical and stroke, which CLDR 48.2.0's root.xml (collation private-unihan) names "the CLDR collation root table's radical-stroke order", and the archived CollationTest files hold only Han characters that order alike by that order and by the UCA's implicit weights; the answer moves with the order of Han characters, which UTS #35 Part 5 (CLDR 48) leaves to the implementation ("an implementation may choose either to implement the order defined in the UCA and the [Unified_Ideograph] data, or to implement the order defined by the [radical ...] lines"), and which ECMA-402 does not fix: out is the reference's, by radical and stroke; each engine's expectation is its own collation data's answer (the owner's decision of 2026-11-02, JSD-0084): Broiler.VM's, its tables' UCA 17 implicit weights over allkeys_CLDR.txt (ref:ucaimplicit@1), and Broiler.JS's, its host's ICU by radical and stroke, which is out; neither is a correction, and finding F1 stays open for SJL-17.3 (row O3, data policy, C5)
since: 33

id: intl/collation/root/han/0002
area: intl
op: Intl.Collator.prototype.compare
in: str:"en" str:"\u4E01" str:"\u4E02"
out: value: str:"<"
class: normative
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1 ref:ucaimplicit@1
script: ["<","=",">"][Math.sign(new Intl.Collator("en").compare("\u4E01","\u4E02"))+1]
note: U+4E01 against U+4E02 under en: row O3 (data policy, C5): Han across blocks (finding F1): the reference orders them by radical and stroke, which CLDR 48.2.0's root.xml (collation private-unihan) names "the CLDR collation root table's radical-stroke order", and the archived CollationTest files hold only Han characters that order alike by that order and by the UCA's implicit weights; the UCA's implicit weights over CLDR 48.2.0's allkeys_CLDR.txt give the same answer (ref:ucaimplicit@1), so it holds under either Han order UTS #35 Part 5 (CLDR 48) allows
since: 33

