in: str:"en" str:"\uF900" str:"\u8C48"
out: value: str:"="
class: normative
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.collator.prototype.compare spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-collator-comparestrings ref:intlref@1 ref:ucaimplicit@1
script: ["<","=",">"][Math.sign(new Intl.Collator("en",{sensitivity:"base"}).compare("\uF900","\u8C48"))+1]
note: U+F900 against U+8C48 under en {sensitivity:"base"}: row O3 (data policy, C5): Han across blocks (finding F1): the reference orders them by radical and stroke, which CLDR 48.2.0's root.xml (collation private-unihan) names "the CLDR collation root table's radical-stroke order", and the archived CollationTest files hold only Han characters that order alike by that order and by the UCA's implicit weights; the UCA's implicit weights over CLDR 48.2.0's allkeys_CLDR.txt give the same answer (ref:ucaimplicit@1), so it holds under either Han order UTS #35 Part 5 (CLDR 48) allows
since: 33

